    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Escape Sequences"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Suppose, we want to print a string like this:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "\"What's there?\", asked Paul"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Since there are quotation marks in it, we have to use \\' to indicate ' and \\\" to indicate \". For example,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1text = \"\\\"What\\'s there?\\\", asked Paul\"\n2print(text)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "\"What's there?\", asked Paul"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, \\' and \\\" are called escape sequences. They allow us to include special characters in strings."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Another commonly used escape sequence is \\n, which is used for newline (next line)."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1print(\"Hey\\nHello\\nHowdy?\")"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Hey\nHello\nHowdy?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "As you can see, when \\n is encountered, it's treated as a newline."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
    },
